  "worked_solution": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{3} & =|u\\cdot v|+\u2016u+v\u2016 \\\\  & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot \u2016v\u2016+\u2016u+v\u2016 \\\\  & =\u2016u\u2016\\cdot (2\\sqrt{3})+\u2016u+v\u2016 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\u2016u\u2016+\u2016u+v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}\u2016u\u2016+\u2016u+v\u2016 & \\le 2\\sqrt{3}\u2016u\u2016+(\u2016u\u2016+\u2016v\u2016) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\u2016u\u2016+(\u2016u\u2016+2\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{3}+1)\u2016u\u2016+2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{3} & \\le (2\\sqrt{3}+1)\u2016u\u2016+2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 10\\sqrt{3} & \\le (2\\sqrt{3}+1)\u2016u\u2016 \\\\ \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}+1} & \\le \u2016u\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016u\u2016$ is $\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}+1}.$",
